freecell-solver needs its Perl and Python modules in the build interpreters.

CMakeLists.txt checks for Moo with ${PERL_EXECUTABLE}, and the build runs
scripts/gen-*.pl, which load Moo, Path::Tiny and Template. It also checks
that the build python3 can import six, pysol_cards and
pysol_cards.gen_multi_cli. Upstream lists these modules only as DEPENDS,
which in a cross build are target packages; the build interpreters are the
host tools perl and python, so CMake stopped at CMakeLists.txt:246 and then
at CMakeLists.txt:1019. Declare them as TOOL_DEPENDS as well.
Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted); upstream status: not submitted.

--- a/games/freecell-solver/Makefile
+++ b/games/freecell-solver/Makefile
@@ -16,6 +16,14 @@
 DEPENDS+=	p5-Moo-[0-9]*:../../devel/p5-Moo
 DEPENDS+=	p5-Path-Tiny-[0-9]*:../../filesystems/p5-Path-Tiny
 DEPENDS+=	p5-Template-Toolkit-[0-9]*:../../www/p5-Template-Toolkit
+# The CMake step runs Perl generators that load Moo, Path::Tiny and
+# Template with the build perl.
+TOOL_DEPENDS+=	p5-Moo-[0-9]*:../../devel/p5-Moo
+TOOL_DEPENDS+=	p5-Path-Tiny-[0-9]*:../../filesystems/p5-Path-Tiny
+TOOL_DEPENDS+=	p5-Template-Toolkit-[0-9]*:../../www/p5-Template-Toolkit
+# The CMake step checks that the build python imports six and pysol_cards.
+TOOL_DEPENDS+=	${PYPKGPREFIX}-pysol_cards>=0.24.0:../../games/py-pysol_cards
+TOOL_DEPENDS+=	${PYPKGPREFIX}-six-[0-9]*:../../lang/py-six
 
 USE_LANGUAGES=	c c++
 USE_TOOLS+=	gmake perl
